    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0550" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg480"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 20, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of the instructions given by the treasury department of Mexico to the
                    collector at Guaymas, with reference to the permission conceded by this
                    government in Mr. Lerdo de Tejada’s note of the 26th ultimo, for the
                    introduction at the port of Guaymas and the conveyance in transit by land of
                    United States army supplies destined for Arizona.</p>
                <p>A copy of the note of Mr. Lerdo de Tejada, enclosing to me said instructions, is
                    also annexed hereto.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. L. PLUMB.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d351-a1.xml" xpointer="d351-a1"/>
            </div>
